Changes required in the Nexus UI repo (vincemedia/bsvnexus) to bundle it offline.

Applied by hand to apps/ui, which is fetched and gitignored — so these must land upstream
or be re-applied after every `npm run ui:fetch`.

1. next.config.ts — enable static export.

     output: "export",
     trailingSlash: true,
     images: { unoptimized: true, ...existing },

   NOTE: assetPrefix must NOT be set to a relative value. next/font rejects anything that
   is not a leading slash or an absolute URL. Relative asset paths are produced afterwards
   by tools/bundle-ui.mjs rewriting the emitted HTML.

2. app/robots.ts and app/sitemap.ts — add, after the imports:

     export const dynamic = "force-static";

   Without it the export fails: "export const dynamic = force-static / revalidate not
   configured on route /robots.txt with output: export".

Nothing else in the UI needed changing. The browse-pane integration is a separate patch,
tools/ui-integration.patch.
